{%- comment -%}
  The company note under Helio's footer (Krish's ruling, 19 Oct 2026: every business site names
  both companies in a subtle footer note, as its terms and privacy policy do). Helio's footer has
  no field for it, so this section sits last in the footer group, on the footer's own background,
  in smaller, muted type than the copyright line above it. The words are fixed: the exact company
  names only, no numbers, addresses or jurisdictions. Placed by the theme push's
  "footer_company_note" option (.github/scripts/footer-note.mjs).
  Since 21 Oct it also carries the one small "Answers" link Krish approved: Helio's footer renders
  no menu, and the Answers library is unlisted elsewhere (growth-heartside docs/GEO-AEO.md).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .hs-company-note { background: {{ section.settings.background }}; margin-top: -12px; padding: 0 20px 20px; }
  .hs-company-note a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .hs-company-note p {
    margin: 0 auto; max-width: 1200px; text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.6875rem; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: rgb(var(--palette-lightest-rgb, 255 255 255) / var(--opacity-muted-text, 0.6));
  }
</style>
<div class="hs-company-note">
  <p>{%- if section.settings.answers_url != blank -%}<a href="{{ section.settings.answers_url }}">{{ section.settings.answers_label }}</a> · {% endif -%}Heartside is a Mindmaker LLC company. Mindmaker Ltd in the UK.</p>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HS company note",
  "class": "hs-company-note-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "color", "id": "background", "label": "Background (match the footer)", "default": "#0f0f0f" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "answers_label", "label": "Answers link text", "default": "Answers" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "answers_url", "label": "Answers link (a path on this store)", "default": "/blogs/answers" }
  ],
  "enabled_on": { "groups": ["footer"] }
}
{% endschema %}
